    'intro_en' => 'You take off your shoes at the edge of the valley, because the ground itself is holy. From there the path leads down between walnut and olive trees to a cluster of stone courtyards, a bridge crossed three times at a run, two springs no outsider may enter, and three white spires that catch the light from across the hills — the centre of a faith older than its written history.',
